  "notes": "Cash-basis governmental funds (Total Governmental Funds column p4; Eliminations column removes the 656 General-to-Street transfer, so Total prints transfers in 556,539 / out 28,043); choices follow FY2023/FY2024. Fund balance roll-forward 734,796 + 1,080,543 - 1,512,100 + 556,539 - 28,043 = 831,735. Beginning and ending cash null (no single governmental cash total printed; cash lines are in balance_sheet), as in the later years. Property taxes 207,563 (p4) split using the County Treasurer Activity schedule (p13), whose total revenues collected equal it exactly. Sales and other taxes 121,518 split by fund column only: Street 17,077 equals the budget schedule's 'Motor vehicle tax' (p8); the General Fund 104,441 is not broken down (budget sales tax 92,062 + other state receipts 3,198 do not add to it), kept with dominant sales tax and review. Fees, taxes, permits and licenses split by fund column (Street 11,442 = budget 'Motor vehicle fees'). Grant proceeds federal: budget 'Federal receipts' 133,646 = federal shared receipts 95,927 + grant proceeds 37,719 (p8). County treasurer 'Interest' 1,399 recorded as Interest Income (page does not say it is interest on taxes). Business-type 'Other' revenue kept other: the Statement of Activities (p2) counts it in Miscellaneous (business-type Charges for Services 1,817,730 = Sales only). Business-type accrual (net position): 2,688,593 + 1,840,946 - 1,200,235 - 528,496 = 2,800,808. Proprietary cash flows null as in the later years (cash-basis report; p7 prints operating 944,519, noncapital (528,496), capital (202,209), investing 432, cash 584,171 -> 798,417). Detail: County Treasurer schedule (p13) and the four utility schedules (pp9-12, which sum to the proprietary statement); no governmental statement-column lines (as in the later years); the all-funds budget comparison (p8) is combined governmental+utility and not recorded. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}
